LAST_SUCCESS=wart-arbiter-power (5aa52868) + class-based doze policy (dabddd76) DONE + device-verified + pushed. Doze is arbiter-decided (PowerModule, screen poller, 60s grace), host-applied (dumb applier, ime_inbound Doze). Per-app cadence by class: bg-service→10s maintenance, normal→60s suspend. Class via report-power-class (host reads manifest background flag, reports; arbiter owns — "host reads/reports, arbiter owns/decides", NOT arbiter parsing manifest = future PackageManager). Verified: Signal→doze 10000, launcher→doze 60000. 5 arbiter modules: wm/shell/alarm/notify/power.
NOTES=Power follow-ups: user-set per-app profiles (restricted/optimized/unrestricted — needs a settings store/UI), wakelock exemptions (suppress doze), maintenance-window alarm batching, deep-doze via SoC wakelock+RTC (boot-model era). Known gap: host launched mid-doze defaults normal until next transition (fan on-change). Power-key-to-sleep via injected keyevent doesn't work (wart input focus grabs it; physical button works). Device: 2-min timeout, AOD disabled. Roadmap: lockscreen/Keyguard, Clipboard(task42), PackageManager perms, Signal app features, boot-model(33), Hybrid(46), WasmGC leak(25). Audio-focus deferred until driver. Plan: ~/.claude/plans/cat-task-state-steady-stallman.md.
